From d482589c44399c6660b63002a99cd6474ce5931c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:49:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] execute_code: sandbox terminal() returns the
 complete output, not the chat window

A script that wrote terminal(...)["output"] to disk as data got the
head+tail window sized for the chat (tool_output.max_bytes) with the
"[OUTPUT TRUNCATED - N chars omitted out of M total]" marker in the middle
and exit_code 0 (self-heal defect agent-7ac9c5fa93: a SHA256SUMS manifest
shipped 49,872 of 63,562 chars).

- code_execution_rpc: host-side, for every transport (UDS, remote file RPC,
  session kernels), a sandbox terminal() result whose window overflowed now
  carries the full text from the terminal spill file (already ANSI-stripped
  and redacted; read cap 20 MB) and truncated: false. When the spill is
  missing, unreadable or itself capped, the window stays and truncated: true
  with full_output_path.
- environments/base + terminal_tool_result: the spill file no longer keeps
  the session's __HERMES_PIPE_/__HERMES_CWD_ marker lines the rendered
  window already drops.
- execute_code schema + stub docstring document output as complete and the
  truncated flag (prompt-surface snapshot re-rendered).
- write_file: content containing a Hermes truncation notice still writes but
  returns a "warning" (and logs it) naming the truncation marker.

Red on 44a29a7f4e3: tests/tools/test_code_execution_terminal_full_output.py
(len 49,823 != 140,127; missing truncated/warning keys).
